      "id": "idea",
      "narration": "You might watch someone pour their last savings into lottery tickets and think they are being foolish. But a person who grew up with nothing may see that ticket as the only shot they will ever get at a different life. To them, it is not crazy at all. It is hope. Every one of us makes money decisions based on our own small slice of experience, and that slice feels like the whole world.",
